  "tagline": "One of the original relational databases, still sold by Actian for long-lived enterprise systems.",
  "description": "Ingres grew out of the 1970s Berkeley research project that also spawned Postgres, Sybase and SQL Server lineages, and it remains a commercial RDBMS maintained by Actian, part of HCLSoftware. Today's Actian Ingres (which absorbed the former Actian X, combining Ingres OLTP with the Vector columnar engine for analytics) targets organizations with decades-old Ingres and OpenROAD applications, adding modern pieces such as at-rest encryption, TLS 1.3, CDC via a Log Reader API, containers and Kubernetes deployment, and cloud hosting through the Ingres NeXt program. It is a sensible platform for keeping legacy estates supported, rarely a choice for new projects.",
